{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 at ~48.5% accuracy), the dominant uncertainty is which modality carries the most discriminative signal. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly compares the image modality against the RNA baseline while holding profile_setting constant, isolating the modality effect. If image_only substantially outperforms rna_only, the search should pivot toward image-centric and multimodal configurations; if it performs comparably or worse, RNA-based improvements (better encoders, multiprofile) become the priority. This is the highest-impact, highest-uncertainty design decision in the space, and resolving it first maximizes the information gained per experiment under a tight budget."
}

